  "text": {
    "id": {
      "title": "Min heap",
      "story": "Buat class `MinHeap`, yaitu binary heap yang disimpan di satu array. Elemen terkecil selalu ada di indeks 0, dan anak dari indeks `i` ada di `2i + 1` dan `2i + 2`.\nMetode: `insert(x)`, `peek()` yang mengembalikan elemen terkecil tanpa mengambilnya, `extractMin()` yang mengambil elemen terkecil, dan `size()`. `peek` dan `extractMin` mengembalikan `null` kalau heap kosong. Jangan pakai `sort`.",
      "hint1": "`insert`: taruh elemen di akhir array, lalu tukar dengan induknya (indeks `(i - 1) >> 1`) selama elemen itu lebih kecil.",
      "hint2": "`extractMin`: simpan elemen di indeks 0, pindahkan elemen terakhir ke indeks 0, lalu tukar ke bawah dengan anak yang lebih kecil selama anak itu lebih kecil."
    },
    "en": {
      "title": "Min heap",
      "story": "Build a `MinHeap` class: a binary heap stored in one array. The smallest element is always at index 0, and the children of index `i` sit at `2i + 1` and `2i + 2`.\nMethods: `insert(x)`, `peek()` which returns the smallest element without removing it, `extractMin()` which removes and returns it, and `size()`. `peek` and `extractMin` return `null` when the heap is empty. No `sort`.",
      "hint1": "`insert`: put the element at the end of the array, then swap it with its parent (index `(i - 1) >> 1`) while it's smaller.",
      "hint2": "`extractMin`: save index 0, move the last element to index 0, then swap it down with its smaller child while that child is smaller."
    }
  },
